{"availability":"available","full":"ocavue/aria-ui","name":"aria-ui","description":"Unstyled Light-DOM-Only Web Components","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":20,"forks":1,"created":"2024-02-24T16:12:12Z","updated":"2026-10-07T06:13:30Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://aria-ui.pages.dev","topics":[],"demo":"https://aria-ui.pages.dev/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T14:47:19.182Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T14:47:19.182Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T14:47:19.182Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T14:47:19.182Z","stars":20,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Aria UI is a monorepo of focused, composable packages. Every component is a native light-DOM custom element, so it works in plain HTML, in any framework, and with any styling solution you already use."],"features":["Light DOM only. No Shadow DOM, so global CSS, Tailwind, and [aria-] / [data-] selectors all work directly.","Unstyled by design. Components ship zero CSS and expose their state through standard ARIA attributes and a few data- hooks for you to style however you like.","Built on the WAI-ARIA APG. Roles, focus management, and keyboard interactions follow the WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices Guide.","Framework-agnostic. Use the elements directly in HTML, or generate idiomatic wrappers with @aria-ui/cli.","Composable parts. Each component is split into focused custom elements (-root, -trigger, -popup, -positioner, -item, …) that talk to each other through a shared store."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ocavue/aria-ui/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"8ce6e2f5afb0b0410e8c69c4e107ff04fb145d1b2ac6f2d61ccb8f8b7a43ac36","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T14:47:19.344Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T14:47:19.344Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Aria UI is a monorepo of focused, composable packages. Every component is a native light-DOM custom element, so it works in plain HTML, in